Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0a0cec05-12f6-4190-8345-55ab22cc8f6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Primary goal to introduce non-commuting coefficients at basis elements of \
Clifford algebra is to enable computations on tensor product of two (this is \
restriction) Clifford algebras. In general it is known that tensor product of \
arbitrary Clifford algebras is not a Clifford algebra, (see N. G. Marchuk\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
    "Classification", " ", "of", " ", "Extended", " ", "Clifford", " ", 
     "Algebras"}], "Author",
    StripOnInput->False,
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
   Appearance->"Frameless",
   ButtonFunction:>SystemOpen[
     FileNameJoin[{
       ParentDirectory[
        NotebookDirectory[
         EvaluationNotebook[]]], "ElectronicHandBook", "BibliographySources", 
       "Articles", 
       "Marchuk_2018_Classification_of_Extended_Clifford_Algebras.pdf"}]],
   Evaluator->Automatic,
   Method->"Preemptive"]], "Output",
  GeneratedCell->False,
  CellAutoOverwrite->False,ExpressionUUID->
  "d97bbacc-6d44-4ad5-8634-8dc20567c203"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], (2018), Proceedings of the Steklov Institute of \
Mathematics. Vol.  62, No 11, pp. 11-23.). By introducing new \
CommutativeProduct, we believe it now possible to compute also in algebras \
with multiple imaginary units as well. This notebook is intended to \
demonstrate some of possibilities"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00d0999d-61f7-416f-bf9c-34ddd972481b"]
}, Open  ]],

