Cell["\<\
So, we can use as a basis algebra Cl(2,0) and as the coefficient algebra the \
algebra Cl(0,2) (this is preferable since Cl(0,2) is a noncommutative field, \
quaternions) or use  Cl(0,2)  as base Clifford algebra and Cl(2,0) as field. \
We will use the later possibility (since the former at the moment requires \
modification of gaDefineOrthonormalBasis for TensorProduct.) First,  we \
define basis for initial Clifford algebra\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4458a88e-5011-420a-8a54-15dadf7652a7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

